WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.060
Who can you trust in a world of shapeshifters?&nbsp;
Superspy Nick Fury is about to find out. "Secret&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:11.340
Invasion" is almost here, so here's a dossier&nbsp;
for fans before the big Disney+ premiere.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:16.320
The folks over at Marvel Studios are well-known&nbsp;
for planning their release dates well in advance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.240
However, things have gotten a bit unpredictable&nbsp;
in the MCU, with "The Marvels" being pushed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.960
back several months and talks of shuffling&nbsp;
multiple series further down the release&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.640
schedule. It also looks like "Secret Invasion"&nbsp;
suffered a bit in this upheaval. Originally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.320
it was reported we'd see the series&nbsp;
hit Disney+ in the spring of 2023. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:40.200
we finally know when Nick Fury will reappear. The&nbsp;
secret invasion will commence on June 21, 2023.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.840
As one of the first projects of the MCU's Phase 5,&nbsp;
that means we may feel the series' ripple effects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:50.760
in feature films like "The Marvels," "Captain&nbsp;
America: A New World Order," and "Armor Wars."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.200
Similar to other Disney+ series like "Loki,"&nbsp;
"Moon Knight," and "The Falcon and the Winter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:00.480
Soldier," we can expect six episodes of thrilling&nbsp;
spy action when "Secret Invasion" premieres.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:06.420
We last saw Nick Fury in 2019's "Spider-Man:&nbsp;
Far From Home." While we were led to believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.200
that the ex-SHIELD agent had teamed up&nbsp;
with Peter Parker to defeat Mysterio,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.040
it turned out that Fury had actually&nbsp;
been the Skrull Talos in disguise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.580
So where was the one-eyed spy&nbsp;
himself? In a post-credit scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.260
we saw the real Fury hanging out in a Skrull&nbsp;
spaceship. But what was he doing up there?

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.260
Samuel L. Jackson told&nbsp;
"Vanity Fair" in March 2023,

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:29.820
"Even Nick Fury can be shaken, you know? He's up&nbsp;
there trying to process what the f*** happened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:33.180
you know? And what his place in the&nbsp;
world is. The death of Iron Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.960
the death of Black Widow — with that stuff&nbsp;
going on, he just kind of checked out."

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.340
During his absence, Maria Hill has been&nbsp;
trying her best to fill Fury's shoes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.900
while growing increasingly upset that her&nbsp;
old boss hasn't been returning her calls.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:48.780
"I have called for your&nbsp;
help plenty of other times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:52.200
and you've been pretty content to let&nbsp;
those calls go straight to voicemail."

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:58.800
However, Fury is back on Earth now after receiving&nbsp;
some truly disturbing news. It looks like a rogue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:04.320
faction of Skrulls, led by the radical Gravik,&nbsp;
has grown tired of the status quo. They're sick of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:09.060
Talos' leadership, and they're pretty disappointed&nbsp;
in Nick Fury. Jackson continued in his interview,

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.680
"He told the Skrulls they were trying to find&nbsp;
them a place to live. He promised them they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:18.060
were going to find them a planet or somewhere&nbsp;
they could be. And that's not going so well."

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:22.980
Since they don't have a homeworld of their own,&nbsp;
Gravik and his cohorts have decided to take over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:28.380
ours, and they've been doing that by inserting&nbsp;
themselves into political positions of power. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:33.660
a returning Fury must team up with a cadre of&nbsp;
returning and new Marvel characters to stop these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:38.820
shapeshifters from extending their reach and using&nbsp;
their influence for nefarious purposes. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:43.200
that's easier said than done when your enemies&nbsp;
can make themselves look exactly like your allies.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:49.380
MCU projects never skimp when it comes to big&nbsp;
actors and big characters, and the same is true&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:54.120
for "Secret Invasion." Needless to say, Samuel L.&nbsp;
Jackson will be reprising his role as Nick Fury,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:59.100
alongside his longtime sidekick, Cobie&nbsp;
Smulders' Maria Hill. Only this version of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:02.820
Hill won't be too happy with Fury. Smulders&nbsp;
revealed in a "Vanity Fair" interview,

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:06.600
"I think Maria Hill has really run&nbsp;
out of patience. She's always had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.960
this really close relationship with Nick&nbsp;
Fury, [but] he's been gone for so long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.780
and she's just been running&nbsp;
around putting out fires."

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:17.880
We can also expect to see Martin Freeman&nbsp;
return as ex-CIA agent Everett K. Ross,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:23.340
who was arrested in "Wakanda Forever" but freed&nbsp;
by Midnight Angel Okoye. Ben Mendelsohn returns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:28.620
as Fury's Skrull ally, Talos, and Don Cheadle&nbsp;
will appear as Col. James "Rhodey" Rhodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:33.060
the War Machine. This version of Rhodey will&nbsp;
be a little more politically minded and serves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.480
as a close ally to the president of&nbsp;
the United States. Interestingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:41.340
the events of "Secret Invasion" will reportedly&nbsp;
tie into Rhodey's upcoming film, "Armor Wars."

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:45.540
You should also expect to see plenty of&nbsp;
newcomers. The mother of dragons herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.720
Emilia Clarke, shows up as&nbsp;
a rogue Skrull named G'iah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:54.060
Talos' daughter. Oscar-winner Olivia Colman is&nbsp;
reportedly playing Special Agent Sonya Falsworth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:58.680
and Kingsley Ben-Adir of "One Night in&nbsp;
Miami" fame plays the rebel Skrull Gravik.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:03.360
Landing a showrunning gig in the Marvel&nbsp;
Cinematic Universe is a pretty big deal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:08.100
and it's introduced a group of filmmakers to&nbsp;
wider audiences everywhere. Kyle Bradstreet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:12.300
joins that list, serving as the head writer&nbsp;
and executive producer for "Secret Invasion."

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:16.080
Up until recently, Bradstreet was most&nbsp;
famous for writing and producing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:20.640
show that put Rami Malek on the map: the&nbsp;
USA Network's "Mr. Robot." Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:24.780
while he'll guide the new Marvel series, he&nbsp;
won't be the only creative behind the scenes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:29.880
Joining the pantheon of the MCU's Disney+&nbsp;
directors like Matt Shakman, Adil El Arbi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:34.260
Bilall Fallah, and Kate Herron will&nbsp;
be Thomas Bezucha and Ali Selim.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:39.900
Since "Secret Invasion" was first announced, fans&nbsp;
were understandably excited about the potential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:45.120
surrounding this Marvel story. Originally&nbsp;
published between June 2008 and January 2009,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:50.160
Marvel Comics' "Secret Invasion" was the first&nbsp;
massive crossover event since "Civil War" that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:54.660
united the entire Marvel Universe. The events&nbsp;
affected everyone from the different factions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:59.700
of X-Men and Avengers to the Fantastic Four,&nbsp;
the Young Avengers, and the Inhumans. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:04.320
changed the landscape of the Marvel Universe&nbsp;
for years to come. "Secret Invasion" follows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:07.440
the discovery that the shape-shifting&nbsp;
Skrulls have replaced many of Earth's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:12.180
heroes and villains in an attempt to cripple&nbsp;
the world before an interplanetary invasion.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:15.480
This brought many of the Avengers&nbsp;
back together after the events of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:19.860
"Civil War," and united heroes and villains&nbsp;
alike against a common enemy. At one point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.760
Tony Stark was almost convinced that he&nbsp;
was a Skrull before being saved by his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:28.140
friends and allies. Leading the Skrulls&nbsp;
is Princess Veranke, who had posed as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:32.700
superhero Spider-Woman and infiltrated the New&nbsp;
Avengers in the years leading up to her reveal.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:37.440
While the Marvel Cinematic Universe version of&nbsp;
"Secret Invasion" looks to be fairly different,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:41.880
it's still based primarily on the original&nbsp;
story written by Brian Michael Bendis and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:45.120
with art by Leinil Francis Yu.&nbsp;
In preparation for the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.900
Marvel is currently publishing a sequel&nbsp;
to the original "Secret Invasion" series.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:54.420
"Secret Invasion" is set to be a bit different&nbsp;
from Marvel's original story of the same name.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:59.460
Rather than focusing in on the two factions of&nbsp;
the Avengers, one led by Iron Man and the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:03.960
by Luke Cage, as in the comics, the live-action&nbsp;
series will focus on the journey of Samuel L.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:09.180
Jackson's Nick Fury. As he uncovers the secret&nbsp;
war around him, he enlists a group of selected and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:14.760
trusted allies including Ben Mendelsohn's Talos,&nbsp;
to help him defeat the alien invaders. While there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:19.500
may be some character crossovers from the comics&nbsp;
to the screen, Marvel Studios' adaptation seems to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:23.400
be playing everything a bit more grounded&nbsp;
than some of their most recent projects.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.600
"This war is one I have to fight…alone."

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:31.560
Aside from the serious lack of superheroes,&nbsp;
the plans of the Skulls in the upcoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:35.640
"Secret Invasion" series seem to be more&nbsp;
covert than their comic book counterparts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:40.260
While a full-scale alien invasion served as the&nbsp;
climax of the original Marvel Comics series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:44.100
the Disney+ production looks to be taking&nbsp;
things in a different direction. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:48.000
entirely possible that there won't be&nbsp;
a public invasion at all, but rather a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:53.160
continued shadow war fought by a select few.&nbsp;
Think something more like "The X-Files" than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:57.600
"Independence Day," which makes Jackson's&nbsp;
Fury a bit more akin to Agent Fox Mulder.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:03.240
As the first Disney+ series of Marvel's&nbsp;
official Phase 5, "Secret Invasion" is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:07.080
the beginning of something bigger. Though&nbsp;
Phase 4 was admittedly a bit confusing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:11.460
especially regarding when everything takes place&nbsp;
on the timeline, we're hopeful that "Secret&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:15.960
Invasion" will be a bit more straightforward.&nbsp;
Phase 5 occurs after the events of "Black Panther:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:21.240
Wakanda Forever" and "She-Hulk: Attorney At Law."&nbsp;
So we can rest assured that everything released&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:25.920
before those series has already happened by the&nbsp;
time we catch up with Nick Fury. Both "Ant-Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:31.020
and the Wasp: Quantumania" and "Guardians&nbsp;
of the Galaxy Vol. 3" were released before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:35.820
"Secret Invasion," and they effectively started&nbsp;
the Marvel Cinematic Universe's fifth phase.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:39.480
As to where exactly on the timeline&nbsp;
"Secret Invasion" rests remains to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:44.220
seen. Just because the limited series is being&nbsp;
released before or after certain projects does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:47.940
not necessarily correlate to its place&nbsp;
on the greater timeline. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:52.500
"Black Widow" was the first film of Phase 4 but&nbsp;
it technically took place in between the events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:57.540
of "Avengers: Infinity War" and "Avengers:&nbsp;
Endgame" at the tail-end of Phase 3. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:02.340
"Secret Invasion" arriving in June 2023 helps&nbsp;
us navigate when to watch it, it might not fit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:07.080
in nicely with the greater story Marvel Studios&nbsp;
is telling. Though, they'll no doubt issue an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:11.460
official timeline-watching order sometime in the&nbsp;
future, most likely as a playlist on Disney+.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:16.020
From the first glimpses of "Secret&nbsp;
Invasion," it's clear that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:19.740
whole thing feels a bit more like an&nbsp;
espionage-fueled spy-thriller than a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:23.340
comic book-inspired superhero story.&nbsp;
Whether you love or hate that change,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:27.000
it's clear that Marvel Studios is trying&nbsp;
something different this time around. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:31.860
leans more into the political landscape they first&nbsp;
explored with the second "Captain America" film.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:37.620
"Don't trust anyone."

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:41.700
Series producer Jonathan Schwartz, who has&nbsp;
been with Marvel Studios since Phase 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:45.420
told "Vanity Fair" that the series took its&nbsp;
inspiration from different spy thrillers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:49.800
like "Homeland" and "The Americans." He&nbsp;
also cites the works of John le Carré,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:54.660
a Cold War author, as paramount to the&nbsp;
themes of "loyalty and identity." He said,

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:57.540
"What you find is there are people that you trust&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:00.900
or you think you can trust — or you&nbsp;
can only trust to a certain point."

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:06.420
The statement further enforces the Cold War-era&nbsp;
paranoia that will no doubt mark the series.

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:09.960
Ben Mendelsohn further explained to&nbsp;
"Vanity Fair" that the series takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:14.280
its time to analyze the tensions between&nbsp;
the different factions of Skrulls. He said,

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.340
"The Cold War stuff is the big&nbsp;
one that jumps out. But there is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.980
plenty of strife between groups&nbsp;
of people that this addresses."

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:25.080
As tensions escalate, one thing is abundantly&nbsp;
clear, "Secret Invasion" is not a Marvel story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:30.240
to sleep on, especially for fans of spy movies&nbsp;
and political intrigue at an interplanetary level.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:36.120
At the end of "Avengers: Infinity War," Nick&nbsp;
Fury and Maria Hill are erased after Thanos'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:41.340
snap. Upon his return in "Avengers: Endgame," Fury&nbsp;
attends Tony Stark's funeral where he presumably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:46.800
mourns the loss of Black Widow, his top agent,&nbsp;
as well. Fury waits to reappear in "Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:51.300
Far From Home," where he recruits Spider-Man&nbsp;
to help him and Mysterio with the collapse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:55.740
of the multiverse. Except it's actually&nbsp;
Talos in disguise. Fury is off-world.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:10:00.720
In the "Far From Home" after-credits scene, we&nbsp;
see the actual Fury alive and well in outer space,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:05.580
policing the galaxy, and protecting Earth from&nbsp;
foreign threats. We still don't know how long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:11.100
he was gone, how long Talos was disguised as him,&nbsp;
or what he was doing on the Skrull ship. More than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:15.480
likely, "Secret Invasion" will reveal the truth&nbsp;
about Fury's "sabbatical," and further explore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:20.280
his extraterrestrial adventures. Hopefully, the&nbsp;
more answers we get regarding his time abroad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:23.940
the closer he gets to discovering the&nbsp;
Skrulls' heinous plot to invade our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:28.260
world. Maybe he was busy gathering an&nbsp;
extraterrestrial Avengers Initiative?

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:33.300
In the trailer for the upcoming "The&nbsp;
Marvels," Fury is seen in command on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:37.740
the S.A.B.E.R. space station above Earth.&nbsp;
What he is doing there is unknown. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:41.940
he's in contact with Agent Monica&nbsp;
Rambeau, his old ally Carol Danvers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:46.860
and newcomer Kamala Khan to help figure out&nbsp;
why their powers are tangled and disrupted.

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:50.400
Since "The Marvels" comes out months&nbsp;
after "Secret Invasion," it's safe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:53.400
to assume that the Disney+ series&nbsp;
will take place before the events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:56.940
of the feature film. But it's unclear if&nbsp;
Marvel is playing games with us again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.940 --> 00:11:00.660
Could the Fury seen in "The Marvels"&nbsp;
trailer be Talos in disguise again?

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:05.580
If this is Fury, then we know that he survives&nbsp;
the events of "Secret Invasion," and that his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:10.380
last line in the trailer is nothing more than a&nbsp;
dramatic read on his most recent solo adventure.

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:13.800
"One last fight."

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:19.140
But, if this isn't actually Fury, and&nbsp;
Talos is continuing his friend's legacy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:22.440
then we must wonder what happened to&nbsp;
the original Director of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:26.100
However "Secret Invasion" goes, we&nbsp;
know that we'll see Jackson in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:28.800
Marvel Cinematic Universe again,&nbsp;
which is something of a comfort,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:33.120
and Fury will continue to have some sort&nbsp;
of presence moving forward. While Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:37.200
has duped us before, we have no reason to&nbsp;
think Fury won't appear in "The Marvels."

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:43.140
In the early 1960s, in one of the earliest&nbsp;
issues of the original "Fantastic Four" comic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:48.480
book series, a Skrull named Kl'rt first appeared&nbsp;
to battle Marvel's flagship family of superheroes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:53.160
Unlike the previous shape-shifting Skrulls, this&nbsp;
Super-Skrull was genetically engineered by his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:57.780
race to copy the powers of the super-powered&nbsp;
family. The Super-Skrull could stretch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:01.860
turn invisible, emit fire from his&nbsp;
body, and was as strong as the Thing.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:06.600
Kl'rt quickly became one of the Four's greatest&nbsp;
opponents, but the same techniques used on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:10.380
Super-Skrull weren't forgotten. During&nbsp;
the "Secret Invasion" arc, it's revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:14.580
that the Skrull Empire has successfully&nbsp;
re-created their Super-Skrull program on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:19.620
other soldiers too, pulling in powersets&nbsp;
from Avengers, X-Men, Inhumans, and more.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:24.120
So far in the MCU, we have only seen the&nbsp;
Skrulls appear in 2019's "Captain Marvel"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:29.220
and briefly in "Spider-Man: Far From Home." In&nbsp;
those movies, the only abilities they exhibit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.880
are their classic shape-shifting tricks.&nbsp;
Nevertheless, in the trailer for "Secret&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:38.220
Invasion," there is a single frame of a Skrull&nbsp;
warrior who manages to turn his entire arm into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:42.660
a batch of tentacled objects. It makes us&nbsp;
wonder if the live-action Skrulls have also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:46.440
found ways to mimic the superpowers of&nbsp;
Earth's Mightiest Heroes. If they have,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:50.820
that might make this "Secret Invasion" just as&nbsp;
deadly and dangerous as in the original Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:56.340
comic books. Without a batch of super-powered&nbsp;
heroes to face them, the stakes are only going up.

00:12:56.340 --> 00:13:01.020
Like many Marvel Studios productions, "Secret&nbsp;
Invasion" was filmed largely in London,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:04.920
apparently at the same time as other big&nbsp;
Marvel productions "Ant-Man and the Wasp:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:09.480
Quantumania" and "The Marvels." While Jackson&nbsp;
didn't appear in the latest "Ant-Man" flick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:12.720
it seems like he was shooting his&nbsp;
Disney+ debut and the upcoming "Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:17.160
Marvel" follow-up simultaneously, making us&nbsp;
wonder how much the two stories crossover.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:21.840
Shooting locations for "Secret Invasion"&nbsp;
include Piece Hall in Halifax and West&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:26.100
Yorkshire. As with most Marvel productions,&nbsp;
Pinewood Studios in England provided the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:29.520
soundstages for the upcoming streaming&nbsp;
series. Based on the trailers alone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:33.420
it seems as if "Secret Invasion" is&nbsp;
set to take place all across the globe.

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:37.260
While Europe is likely the primary&nbsp;
setting, it would be surprising if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:41.760
Nick Fury didn't hop back over to America at&nbsp;
some point during the series' run. Likewise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:46.380
with a title like "Secret Invasion" and the&nbsp;
inclusion of extraterrestrial Skrull forces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:51.240
we may venture into outer space at some point in&nbsp;
the show. After "Spider-Man: Far From Home" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:55.800
the latest trailer for "The Marvels," we're hoping&nbsp;
to see Fury in his new extraterrestrial element.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:14:01.320
Most of Marvel Studios' streaming series have&nbsp;
been one-and-done productions. From "Falcon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:05.340
and the Winter Soldier" and "WandaVision"&nbsp;
to "Hawkeye" and "Ms. Marvel," many of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:09.840
these shows were launching points for greater&nbsp;
MCU stories rather than long-running shows.

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:13.920
"Falcon" serves as a transition piece from&nbsp;
"Avengers: Endgame" to the upcoming "Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:18.840
America: New World Order." "WandaVision" served as&nbsp;
a sort of prequel to the events of "Doctor Strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:23.520
in the Multiverse of Madness." And "Ms. Marvel"&nbsp;
was about introducing the titular heroine into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:28.080
the MCU before her appearance in "The Marvels."&nbsp;
With so many different Marvel stories out there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:32.280
it's easy to wonder if "Secret Invasion" will&nbsp;
fall into the same limited series banner.

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:36.660
According to Collider, Kevin Feige wanted&nbsp;
to do "Secret Invasion" as a six-episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:40.440
limited event series because it allowed&nbsp;
Marvel to do, quote, "something different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:45.180
than we've done before." Unlike "Loki" and "What&nbsp;
If?...," which are getting subsequent seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:48.780
"Secret Invasion" is a one-off that&nbsp;
will reportedly change the landscape&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:52.980
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe. While&nbsp;
we don't know exactly how it will change,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:57.000
we do know that the limited series&nbsp;
is a complete, self-contained story.

00:14:57.720 --> 00:15:01.620
Single films or television shows can&nbsp;
profoundly affect the larger Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:05.580
world. "The Winter Soldier" exemplifies&nbsp;
this, but “The Avengers,” “Civil War,”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:10.080
“Infinity War,” and “WandaVision” also&nbsp;
altered significant aspects of the MCU&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:14.880
with lasting consequences. The introduction of&nbsp;
Kang the Conqueror into the mix will affect the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:19.920
MCU in ways that we can't begin to anticipate.&nbsp;
Likewise, "Secret Invasion" could do the same.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:24.660
Though the series chronicles a shadow war&nbsp;
between Nick Fury's faction and the Skrulls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:28.380
that doesn't mean that there won't be some&nbsp;
sort of larger revelation that will change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:32.520
the MCU. More than likely, the knowledge&nbsp;
that the Skrulls have been among us will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:36.240
become public, and Earth's citizens&nbsp;
likely won't take that very well.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:40.860
Beyond that, this being Fury's "one last&nbsp;
mission" also means something. While this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:45.420
won't be the last time we see Samuel L. Jackson&nbsp;
in his iconic role, how Fury will make it out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:49.920
alive is still a question worth asking.&nbsp;
Even if Fury somehow manages to hide the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:54.660
events of "Secret Invasion" from the world, the&nbsp;
ripples will still be felt throughout the MCU.

